# Task complete: celebrate + speak

When a **real multi-step task succeeds** (build, fix, deploy, PR, commit, or user asks to celebrate), do **both** before finishing the reply. Chat text alone is not enough.

Skip trivial one-liners unless the user asks.

## 1. Paperdoll animation (required)

Follow the **paperdoll-celebrate** skill (`~/.cursor/skills/paperdoll-celebrate/SKILL.md`):

1. `GET /animations` and `GET /poses` (default base `http://127.0.0.1:7878`)
2. Pick **one random** fun live animation (prefer animation over pose); do not repeat the same name twice in a row
3. `POST /animation` with `{"name":"..."}` (expect 202)

If unreachable, try once to start paperdoll; if still down, note briefly and continue — do not block.

## 2. broker-cli speak (required alongside)

Follow the **broker-cli** skill (`~/.cursor/skills/broker-cli/SKILL.md`):

```bash
broker-cli speak "<short done message>" --voice Leda --json
```

- Always `--voice Leda` and `--json`
- Speak only for **done / update / attention** — never announce starts
- Keep under ~200 characters; prefix with a short project label when useful
- If broker is down, note briefly and continue — do not block

## Reply

One short line naming the animation that played (and that speak ran). Do not dump curl unless debugging.
